      content: `Due to the systemic nature of atherosclerosis, arterial lesions are rarely localized to a single territory. Less than 10% of patients presenting for vascular surgery possess normal coronary anatomy, whereas more than 50% suffer from advanced or severe multivessel CAD. Silent myocardial ischemia (manifested by stress-induced wall motion abnormalities in the absolute absence of anginal symptoms) affects up to 28% of this population, while unrecognized myocardial infarction (characterized by resting segmental wall motion defects without an established clinical history) is present in 23% of cases. Furthermore, left ventricular systolic dysfunction (LVSD) is five times more prevalent in vascular patients than in matched control cohorts.`
